  "releaseNotes": "WorkflowForge.Extensions.Resilience.Polly 2.2.0\n\nBREAKING\n- Removed PollyMiddlewareOptions.RateLimiter, PollyRateLimiterSettings and PollyTimeoutSettings.UseOptimisticTimeout. Rate limiting was validated and cloned but never built into a pipeline; Polly v8 timeouts are always cooperative.\n- Bulkhead isolation and rate limiting have been struck from the package description; neither was implemented.\n- AddWorkflowForgePolly(configuration) now defaults to WorkflowForge:Extensions:Polly (PollyMiddlewareOptions.DefaultSectionName) instead of WorkflowForge:Polly, which bound nothing.\n\nFixed\n- The netstandard2.0 asset declares its four BCL dependencies again (Microsoft.Bcl.TimeProvider, Microsoft.Bcl.AsyncInterfaces, System.ComponentModel.Annotations, System.Threading.Tasks.Extensions).\n- The pipeline is now composed from whichever of Retry, Timeout and CircuitBreaker is enabled, honouring BackoffType, UseJitter, SamplingDuration and MinimumThroughput. DefaultTags and EnableDetailedLogging are applied.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/animatlabs/workflow-forge/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#220---2026-09-15",
